course: dictionary
lesson: 14557
title: Sounding it out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Phonetically means in a way that matches the sounds of speech. When you spell a word phonetically, you write it the way it sounds, not the way it is usually spelled. «Spell the word cat phonetically» means write it the way it sounds.
explain: Young writers often spell phonetically. «I wrote bcoz for because, because that is how it sounds to me.» Your teacher then shows you the correct spelling, so you can learn it.
explain: Reading a word phonetically means sounding it out, one sound at a time, until you hear the word. This works for many words, but not all. «We sailed the yacht across the bay.» You cannot sound out yacht, because its letters do not match its sounds.
fact: Phonetically means in a way that matches the sounds of speech.
fact: «Spell it phonetically» means write it the way it sounds.
fact: Phonetically can also mean to do with the sounds of words, not their meaning.
fact: Some words, such as «yacht» and «colonel», cannot be read phonetically.
fact: A phonetic spelling is a useful first try, but teachers then show the correct spelling.
exercise: «Spell the word cat phonetically.» What does phonetically mean here? | With a picture | *In a way that matches the sounds of speech | In alphabetical order | In a loud voice
exercise: Ben writes «bcoz» for «because», sounding it out. What is he doing? | Drawing a picture of the word | *Spelling phonetically, writing it the way it sounds | Copying from a dictionary | Writing in capital letters
exercise: Lily says, «Reading a word phonetically means sounding it out.» What does sounding it out mean? | *Saying each sound in the word, one by one, to hear it | Looking the word up in a book | Spelling it backwards | Reading it silently without making any sounds
test: Which question is about the phonetics of a word? | Where is this word from? | Who wrote this word? | *How does this word sound? | What does this word mean?
test: Kim writes «kwik» for «quick». Why is this a phonetic spelling? | It is written in another language | It is written in capital letters | *It is spelled the way it sounds | It is the correct spelling in every dictionary
exam: Which word cannot be read phonetically? | cat | dog | *colonel | pin
